From d8154c81316382ab16bbfb1a6e492fbcda84b922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chen Minqiang <ptpt52@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 10:48:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: fix kernel panic in tx scheduling on dual-band
 Wi-Fi 6

Commit aeedee5c0a2c ("wifi: mt76: add multi-radio support to tx scheduling")
introduced a loop where the `phy` pointer is updated based on `wcid->phy_idx`
to support routing tx queues to the correct hardware link in Wi-Fi 7 (MLO)
architectures where multiple PHYs share the same mac80211 hardware
structure (`ieee80211_hw`).

However, this breaks dual-band Wi-Fi 6 (non-MLO) architectures (e.g., MT7981)
where each PHY has its own independent `ieee80211_hw` and corresponding
`active_txqs`. In such architectures, when a STA disconnects and its WCID
is reused by another STA on the other band, a stale `txq` can still remain
in the original PHY's active queue.

During processing, `mt76_txq_schedule_list()` pulls the stale `txq`
from `phy0->hw`, discovers the new `wcid` mapping points to `phy1`,
and updates `phy` to `phy1`. It then calls `mt76_txq_dequeue(phy1, ...)`,
which calls `ieee80211_tx_dequeue(phy1->hw, txq)`.

This causes mac80211 to mix pointers from two different `ieee80211_hw`
(local) contexts: `local B` (phy1) and `local A` (phy0). In `codel_dequeue`,
calculating `flow - local->fq.flows` using pointers from two differently
allocated structures produces a pseudo-random out-of-bounds index, leading
to a memory corruption / kernel panic.

Fix this by ensuring we only update the `phy` pointer if both PHYs share
the same `hw` (MLO). If `phy->hw != wcid_phy->hw`, it indicates a stale
queue from a different MAC, and we safely skip it.

Signed-off-by: Chen Minqiang <ptpt52@gmail.com>
---
 tx.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tx.c b/tx.c
index b863e449d..79eaaeff2 100644
--- a/tx.c
+++ b/tx.c
@@ -572,6 +572,7 @@ mt76_txq_schedule_list(struct mt76_phy *phy, enum mt76_txq_id qid)
 
 	while (1) {
 		int n_frames = 0;
+		struct mt76_phy *wcid_phy;
 
 		txq = ieee80211_next_txq(phy->hw, qid);
 		if (!txq)
@@ -582,7 +583,11 @@ mt76_txq_schedule_list(struct mt76_phy *phy, enum mt76_txq_id qid)
 		if (!wcid)
 			continue;
 
-		phy = mt76_dev_phy(dev, wcid->phy_idx);
+		wcid_phy = mt76_dev_phy(dev, wcid->phy_idx);
+		if (phy->hw != wcid_phy->hw)
+			continue;
+
+		phy = wcid_phy;
 		if (test_bit(MT76_RESET, &phy->state) || phy->offchannel)
 			continue;
 
